course: dictionary
lesson: 3139
title: Elliptical: three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Elliptical is a good example. In maths it describes a shape, in grammar it describes missing words, and in speech it describes talk that is not direct.
explain: In maths, an ellipse is a curved closed shape like a squashed circle. Planets move around the Sun in «elliptical orbits», oval paths rather than perfect circles. The word tells you the shape is stretched, not round.
explain: In grammar, an elliptical sentence leaves out words that the listener can guess. «Coming?» is shorter than «Are you coming?», and both ask the same question. The three dots «…» are also called an ellipsis, because they show that words have been left out.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Galaxies come in main shapes: spirals like ours, round or oval ellipticals, and shapeless irregulars.» The sentence is about shapes, so here elliptical means oval, not missing words.
fact: Elliptical means shaped like an ellipse: a stretched circle or oval.
fact: «Elliptical orbits» are oval paths that planets take around the Sun, not perfect circles.
fact: In grammar, elliptical means leaving out words the listener can guess, as in «Coming?»
fact: «Elliptically» is the adverb: said with words left out, or in a way that is not direct.
fact: In the US, an «elliptical» is also an exercise machine where you move your legs in an oval path.
exercise: «Planets move around the Sun in elliptical orbits.» What does elliptical mean here? | Dark and cold | Round as a football | Very fast | *Oval-shaped, like a stretched circle
exercise: «Are you coming?» can be shortened to «Coming?» Which word describes that shorter way of speaking? | Ancient | Luminous | *Elliptical | Treacherous
exercise: In the US, an elliptical is a machine at the gym. What do you do on it? | *Move your legs in an oval path | Cook your dinner | Lift heavy weights | Swim across a pool
test: What is an ellipsis in grammar? | A very loud noise | A kind of shape with four sides | *Leaving out words the listener can guess | A type of exercise machine
test: «Her answer was elliptical, so I had to think hard about what she meant.» What does elliptical mean here? | Shaped like a circle | Very loud and clear | *Not direct, so hard to understand | Quick and short
exam: Which sentence uses elliptical to mean a shape? | She gave an elliptical reply and left. | Are you coming, then? | *The planet followed an elliptical orbit around the Sun. | Coming?
